# A PDF opened in a tab: the viewer shows its pages drawn (page 1's red
# box, page 2's blue one), its title and page count, finds words through
# the text layer, jumps by the page field, follows a link inside the
# document, and zooms with Ctrl++ / Ctrl+0.
resize 900 700
open pdf-viewer.pdf
advance 500 4
assert-title Viewer Test Document
assert-text / 2
assert-text Sashfold PDF viewer first page
# Page 1 drawn: the red box, the white page around it, the gray behind it.
assert-pixel 280 320 #d91a1a
assert-pixel 120 600 #ffffff
assert-pixel 30 600 #525659
# Find in page reads the text layer.
key ctrl+f
type quick brown
assert-find 1 of 1
key Escape
# The page field: 2 + Enter scrolls page 2 to the top.
click 528 99
type 2
key Enter
advance 500 4
assert-value page 2
assert-pixel 280 320 #1a66d9
# The link on page 2 goes back to page 1.
click-text Back to the first page
advance 500 4
assert-value page 1
assert-pixel 280 320 #d91a1a
# Zoom in one step, then back to automatic.
key ctrl+equal
advance 500 4
assert-value zoom 1.5
key ctrl+0
advance 500 4
assert-value zoom auto
assert-pixel 280 320 #d91a1a
# #zoom=400 from the address: the page wider than the window starts at its
# left edge (it scrolls, not cut off), its picture drawn though over 8 MB.
open pdf-viewer.pdf#zoom=400
advance 500 6
assert-value zoom 4
assert-pixel 450 600 #d91a1a
assert-pixel 200 600 #ffffff
